@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant - the same handshake shown as a timing diagram (state-over-time waveforms) vs a sequence diagram (message order).
'   usecase:      Note the waveform-vs-order viewpoint shift between timing and sequence diagrams.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       Diagram-family comparison
' ============================================================================
title Example Timing Diagram (Variant) - Timing vs Sequence Viewpoint

' A timing diagram answers "WHEN did each participant hold a state?"
' A sequence diagram answers "IN WHAT ORDER were messages exchanged?"
' Same interaction; two different lenses.

robust "Client" as C
robust "Server" as S

@0
C is "Idle"
S is "Listen"
@1
C is "Connecting"
@2
S is "SynRcvd"
@3
C is "Established"
S is "Established"
@8
C is "Closing"
S is "Closed"

note at 3,3
  See the paired sequence diagram below (rendered as a note here
  because a single .puml emits one diagram; the converter splits views).
  Timing view: focus on the waveform each lifeline traces over the time axis.
  Sequence view: focus on the vertical message order, not durations.
end note

@enduml
